{%- comment -%}
  What `quantity` bottles cost at `unit` per bottle under Theme settings → Bundle tiers, in cents.
  The biggest tier the quantity fills applies once (tiers do not repeat): its free bottles cost
  nothing and its discount comes off every bottle that is paid for. So with Buy 2 Get 1 Free and
  Buy 3 Get 3 Free, 4 bottles are charged as 3, and so are 6. This is the Kaching Bundles quantity
  break the tiers mirror; Kaching prices the real cart.

  The buy box prices its bundle cards with it and the cart drawer predicts the next tier with it,
  so the two cannot disagree. Prints the number and nothing else; capture it:
    capture price
      render 'bundle-tier-price', quantity: 4, unit: 3499
    endcapture
  Only a prediction: the drawer always shows what the cart itself says a line costs.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign best_total = 0
  assign best_free = 0
  assign best_discount = 0
  for slot in (1..4)
    assign slot_key = 'bundle_tier_' | append: slot
    assign paid_key = slot_key | append: '_paid'
    assign free_key = slot_key | append: '_free'
    assign discount_key = slot_key | append: '_discount'
    assign slot_paid = settings[paid_key] | default: 0
    if slot_paid > 0
      assign slot_free = settings[free_key] | default: 0
      assign slot_total = slot_paid | plus: slot_free
      if slot_total <= quantity and slot_total > best_total
        assign best_total = slot_total
        assign best_free = slot_free
        assign best_discount = settings[discount_key] | default: 0
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  assign keep = 100 | minus: best_discount
  assign paid_bottles = quantity | minus: best_free
  echo unit | times: keep | divided_by: 100 | times: paid_bottles
-%}
